.TH WREX-ICMP 7 "2026-10-18" "wrex 0.1.0" "wrex Manual"
.SH NAME
wrex-icmp \- icmp layer for \fBwrex\fR(1)

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwrex\fR \fIcraft\fR|\fIsend\fR [options] \fB--layer\fR \fIicmp\fR \fB--icmp\-<field>\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...
\fBwrex\fR \fIfields\fR \fIicmp\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
ICMP (RFC 792) over IPv4. type 0/8 (echo reply/request) expose echo.id and echo.seq plus payload; every other type renders the 4\-byte rest of header as icmp.rest raw bytes. checksum autofilled (explicit wins).
.

.SH ENCAPSULATION
Rank 30; stacks on ipv4 (parents).

.SH "FIELD FLAGS"
Dots in field paths become dashes in flags (ipv4.ttl -> --ipv4-ttl, --icmp-type).
Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept
unvalidated; \fB\-\-strict\fR re-validates (violations exit 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-icmp\-type=\fIINT\fR\fR
type (autofill: 8 echo request) Type u8. Default: 8.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmp\-code=\fIINT\fR\fR
code (autofill: 0) Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmp\-checksum=\fIINT\fR\fR
checksum over header+payload (autofill: computed) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmp\-echo\-id=\fIINT\fR\fR
echo identifier (types 0/8) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmp\-echo\-seq=\fIINT\fR\fR
echo sequence (types 0/8) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-icmp\-rest\fR
raw 4\-byte rest of header (non\-echo types) Type bytes. Default: .

.SH EXAMPLES
wrex craft \-\-format hex \-\-layer eth \-\-layer ipv4 \-\-layer icmp \\\\
  \-\-ipv4\-src=127.0.0.1 \-\-ipv4\-dst=127.0.0.1 \-\-icmp\-type=8 \\\\
  \-\-icmp\-echo\-id=1 \-\-icmp\-echo\-seq=1 \-\-payload=hex:deadbeef

